IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-penalties`
IMPORT `g8-art26-demand`
IMPORT `g8-art27-28-required-steps`
IMPORT `g8-art29-31-information`
IMPORT `ind-c-tests-fixtures-g8`

-- ind-c-tests-art26-31: independent tests (author ind-c) of Part 7, Articles 26 to 31.  Row ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md,
-- decided from the Law before the encoding was opened.  Inputs the encoding needs and the scenario does not fix are stated where they are supplied.

§ `ind-c fixtures for Articles 26 to 31`

GIVEN capacity IS A `Capacity of a person under Article 26(2)`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      formerly IS A BOOLEAN
      whileRegistered IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person addressed by a notice under Article 26`
`ind-c addressee` capacity standing formerly whileRegistered MEANS
    `Person addressed by a notice under Article 26` WITH
        `capacity of the person under Article 26(2)` IS capacity
        `standing of the entity on the register` IS standing
        `the entity was formerly a registered charity` IS formerly
        `governor while the entity was registered` IS whileRegistered

GIVEN purpose IS A `Purpose of a demand for information`
      reasonably IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Demand for information under Article 26(1)`
`ind-c demand` purpose reasonably MEANS
    `Demand for information under Article 26(1)` WITH
        `purpose of the demand` IS purpose
        `the Commissioner reasonably requires what is demanded for that purpose` IS reasonably

GIVETH A `Standing on the register`
`ind-c general` MEANS `entered in the general section`
GIVETH A `Standing on the register`
`ind-c historic` MEANS `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`
GIVETH A `Standing on the register`
`ind-c applicant standing` MEANS `an applicant for registration`

GIVEN retained IS A DATE
      notice IS A DATE
      commenced IS A MAYBE DATE
      concluded IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts of the retention of a document under Article 26(5)`
`ind-c retention` retained notice commenced concluded MEANS
    `Facts of the retention of a document under Article 26(5)` WITH
        `day the document was provided or retained` IS retained
        `day of the notice` IS notice
        `day proceedings were commenced` IS commenced
        `day proceedings concluded` IS concluded

-- A26-22 and following: retained 10 January 2026 under a notice of 5 January 2026.
`ind-c retained 2026-01-10, no proceedings` MEANS `ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) NOTHING NOTHING

GIVEN valid IS A BOOLEAN
      complied IS A BOOLEAN
      privileged IS A BOOLEAN
      excuse IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts of a contravention under Article 26(7)`
`ind-c contravention` valid complied privileged excuse MEANS
    `Facts of a contravention under Article 26(7)` WITH
        `the requirement was validly imposed under Article 26(1) or (4)` IS valid
        `the person did what was required` IS complied
        `what is withheld is subject to legal professional privilege` IS privileged
        `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS excuse

GIVEN compliance IS A BOOLEAN
      againstMaker IS A BOOLEAN
      proceedings IS A `Proceedings in which a statement is tendered`
GIVETH A `Statement made under Article 26`
`ind-c statement` compliance againstMaker proceedings MEANS
    `Statement made under Article 26` WITH
        `made in compliance with a requirement imposed under Article 26` IS compliance
        `tendered against the person who made it` IS againstMaker
        `proceedings` IS proceedings

GIVEN provided IS A BOOLEAN
      known IS A BOOLEAN
      forApplication IS A BOOLEAN
      forNotice IS A BOOLEAN
      inDocument IS A BOOLEAN
      underArticle26 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts of providing information under Article 26(10)`
`ind-c false information` provided known forApplication forNotice inDocument underArticle26 MEANS
    `Facts of providing information under Article 26(10)` WITH
        `the person provided information to the Commissioner` IS provided
        `known by the person to be false in a material particular` IS known
        `intended for an application for registration` IS forApplication
        `intended for deciding whether to serve a required steps notice` IS forNotice
        `contained in a document` IS inDocument
        `provided under Article 26` IS underArticle26

GIVEN provider IS A BOOLEAN
      relevant IS A BOOLEAN
      governorOrEmployee IS A BOOLEAN
      registeredNow IS A BOOLEAN
      formerly IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person asked for an explanation of a document`
`ind-c explainer` provider relevant governorOrEmployee registeredNow formerly MEANS
    `Person asked for an explanation of a document` WITH
        `provided the document` IS provider
        `appears to be in possession of relevant information` IS relevant
        `appears to be a governor or employee of the charity` IS governorOrEmployee
        `the charity is registered now` IS registeredNow
        `the entity was formerly a registered charity` IS formerly

§ `ind-c Article 26 -- the persons and the power`

-- A26-01 .. A26-10: who falls within 26(2)
#ASSERT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `the entity itself` `ind-c general` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `the entity itself` `ind-c historic` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `a governor or former governor of the entity` `ind-c general` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `a governor or former governor of the entity` `ind-c historic` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `the entity itself` `ind-c applicant standing` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `a governor or former governor of the entity` `ind-c applicant standing` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `a person of any other description` `ind-c general` FALSE FALSE)
-- an applicant that was once a registered charity is a formerly registered entity (26(2)(a), src:622)
#ASSERT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `the entity itself` `ind-c applicant standing` TRUE FALSE)
-- F8.17 B (the person must have been a governor while the entity was registered), by that reading's definition
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(2) the person falls within Article 26(2)` `ind-c G8 with F8.17 B` (`ind-c addressee` `a governor or former governor of the entity` `ind-c historic` TRUE FALSE)
-- A26-11, A26-12, A26-14: the power
#ASSERT `Art 26(1) the Commissioner has the power to demand` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `the entity itself` `ind-c general` FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c demand` `determining whether to serve a required steps notice` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 26(1) the Commissioner has the power to demand` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `a governor or former governor of the entity` `ind-c historic` TRUE TRUE) (`ind-c demand` `determining whether to serve a required steps notice` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(1) the Commissioner has the power to demand` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `the entity itself` `ind-c general` FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c demand` `an application for registration` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(1) the Commissioner has the power to demand` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `the entity itself` `ind-c general` FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c demand` `determining whether to serve a required steps notice` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(1) the Commissioner has the power to demand` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c addressee` `the entity itself` `ind-c applicant standing` FALSE FALSE) (`ind-c demand` `determining whether to serve a required steps notice` TRUE)
-- A26-16: a lien survives the provision
#ASSERT `Art 26(3) the effect on a lien of providing the document` TRUE EQUALS `the lien is unaffected by the provision`
-- A26-17 .. A26-19: who may be asked to explain a document provided
#ASSERT `Art 26(4)(a) an explanation of the document may be required of the person` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c explainer` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 26(4)(a) an explanation of the document may be required of the person` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c explainer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(4)(a) an explanation of the document may be required of the person` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c explainer` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§ `ind-c Article 26(5) -- retention for the longer of a year and the proceedings`

-- A26-22 .. A26-25 (A26-24 pre-committed ambiguous: reading A, the anniversary, taken by ind-c)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c retained 2026-01-10, no proceedings` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c retained 2026-01-10, no proceedings` (YMD 2027 1 9)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c retained 2026-01-10, no proceedings` (YMD 2027 1 10)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c retained 2026-01-10, no proceedings` (YMD 2027 1 11)
-- A26-24 reading B (inclusive: the year ends the day before the anniversary)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 with F8.9 B` `ind-c retained 2026-01-10, no proceedings` (YMD 2027 1 10)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 with F8.9 B` `ind-c retained 2026-01-10, no proceedings` (YMD 2027 1 9)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) the Commissioner may keep the document until` `ind-c G8 A` `ind-c retained 2026-01-10, no proceedings` EQUALS `retention is permitted up to and including` (YMD 2027 1 10)
-- A26-26, A26-26b: proceedings commenced within the year, concluded 1 May 2028
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2028 5 1))) (YMD 2027 6 1)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2028 5 1))) (YMD 2028 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2028 5 1))) (YMD 2028 5 2)
-- A26-27: proceedings commenced after the year do not extend it
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2027 2 1)) NOTHING) (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- A26-28: proceedings over within the year; the year is the longer
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1))) (YMD 2026 12 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 4 1))) (YMD 2027 1 11)
-- A26-29: proceedings within the year and not concluded
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) NOTHING) (YMD 2029 1 1)
-- A26-30 (pre-committed ambiguous): proceedings commenced on the anniversary are within the year on reading A, not on reading B
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2027 1 10)) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))) (YMD 2027 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 with F8.9 B` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 1 5) (JUST (YMD 2027 1 10)) (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))) (YMD 2027 5 1)
-- A26-31 (pre-committed ambiguous): retained 29 February 2024
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 20) NOTHING NOTHING) (YMD 2025 2 27)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 20) NOTHING NOTHING) (YMD 2025 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 A` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 20) NOTHING NOTHING) (YMD 2025 3 1)
#ASSERT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 with F8.10 B` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 20) NOTHING NOTHING) (YMD 2025 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 with F8.10 B` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 20) NOTHING NOTHING) (YMD 2025 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 26(5) retention is permitted on` `ind-c G8 with F8.9 B` (`ind-c retention` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2024 2 20) NOTHING NOTHING) (YMD 2025 2 28)
