§ `ind-c Articles 27 and 28 -- required steps notices`

GIVEN registered IS A BOOLEAN
      beliefs IS A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Belief that prompts a required steps notice`
`ind-c grounds` registered beliefs MEANS
    `Art 27(1) the Commissioner has a ground to serve a required steps notice` `ind-c G8 A` registered beliefs FALSE TRUE FALSE (`ind-c plain entity`) FALSE TRUE TRUE

-- An entity record for the rules that take one; nothing in it is read by the reading taken at F8.14.
`ind-c plain entity` MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "Ind-C Plain Entity"
        `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `a company`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS EMPTY

-- A27-01 .. A27-05: each belief is a ground (the Commissioner's belief is the input)
#ASSERT `Art 27(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`ind-c grounds` TRUE (LIST `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`))
#ASSERT `Art 27(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`ind-c grounds` TRUE (LIST `a registered charity does not pass the charity test`))
#ASSERT `Art 27(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`ind-c grounds` TRUE (LIST `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct`))
#ASSERT `Art 27(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`ind-c grounds` TRUE (LIST `a governor of a registered charity is unfit by reason of a reportable matter`))
#ASSERT `Art 27(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`ind-c grounds` TRUE (LIST `a registered charity has ceased to meet the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)`))
-- A27-06: no belief
#ASSERT NOT `Art 27(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`ind-c grounds` TRUE EMPTY)
-- A27-10: not a registered charity
#ASSERT NOT `Art 27(1) paragraph (2) applies` (`ind-c grounds` FALSE (LIST `there has been misconduct by a registered charity`))
-- A27-07 .. A27-09: relevant persons
#ASSERT `Art 27(3) the person is a relevant person` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 27(3) the person is a relevant person` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 27(3) the person is a relevant person` FALSE FALSE
-- A27-12, A27-13: removal or suspension under (1)(c), (1)(d)
#ASSERT `Art 27(4) the steps may include suspension, removal or replacement` `ind-c G8 A` `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct` FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 27(4) the steps may include suspension, removal or replacement` `ind-c G8 A` `a governor of a registered charity is unfit by reason of a reportable matter` FALSE
-- A27-15 (pre-committed ambiguous; reading A taken): not under (1)(a); reading B: yes
#ASSERT NOT `Art 27(4) the steps may include suspension, removal or replacement` `ind-c G8 A` `there has been misconduct by a registered charity` FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 27(4) the steps may include suspension, removal or replacement` `ind-c G8 with F8.15 B` `there has been misconduct by a registered charity` FALSE
-- A27-16: never for an organized religious charity
#ASSERT NOT `Art 27(4) the steps may include suspension, removal or replacement` `ind-c G8 A` `a governor of a registered charity has engaged in misconduct` TRUE

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of requirement in a required steps notice`
GIVETH A `Requirement in a required steps notice`
`ind-c requirement` kind MEANS
    `Requirement in a required steps notice` WITH
        `kind of requirement` IS kind
        `the governor concerned is a governor of the charity` IS TRUE

-- A28-01 .. A28-04: invalid only to the extent of the governor requirement
#ASSERT `Art 28(3) the required steps notice is invalid to the extent` TRUE (`ind-c requirement` `a requirement to remove a governor`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 28(3) the required steps notice is invalid to the extent` TRUE (`ind-c requirement` `any other requirement`)
#ASSERT `Art 28(3) the requirements of the notice that remain valid` TRUE (LIST (`ind-c requirement` `a requirement to remove a governor`), (`ind-c requirement` `any other requirement`)) EQUALS LIST (`ind-c requirement` `any other requirement`)
#ASSERT `Art 28(3) the required steps notice is invalid to the extent` TRUE (`ind-c requirement` `a requirement to suspend a governor`)
#ASSERT `Art 28(3) the required steps notice is invalid to the extent` TRUE (`ind-c requirement` `a requirement to replace a governor`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 28(3) the required steps notice is invalid to the extent` FALSE (`ind-c requirement` `a requirement to remove a governor`)

`ind-c humanist entity` MEANS
    Entity WITH
        name IS "Ind-C Humanist Society"
        `standing on the register` IS `entered in the general section`
        `kinds of entity` IS LIST `an unincorporated body or association of persons`
        `is a Jersey entity` IS TRUE
        governors IS EMPTY
        purposes IS LIST (Purpose WITH description IS "the advancement of humanism", head IS NOTHING, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS TRUE)

-- A28-05 .. A28-09: eligibility to be categorized
#ASSERT `Art 28(1) the charity is eligible to be categorized as an organized religious charity` `ind-c G8 A` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ind-c plain entity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 28(1) the charity is eligible to be categorized as an organized religious charity` `ind-c G8 A` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ind-c plain entity` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 28(1) the charity is eligible to be categorized as an organized religious charity` `ind-c G8 A` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-c plain entity` TRUE
-- A28-09 (pre-committed ambiguous; reading A taken): a philosophical-belief charity is not eligible on A, is on B
#ASSERT NOT `Art 28(1) the charity is eligible to be categorized as an organized religious charity` `ind-c G8 A` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-c humanist entity` TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 28(1) the charity is eligible to be categorized as an organized religious charity` `ind-c G8 with F8.3 B` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ind-c humanist entity` TRUE

GIVEN categorizes IS A BOOLEAN
      discretion IS A BOOLEAN
      granted IS A BOOLEAN
      withdrawn IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity`
`ind-c Article 28 Order` categorizes discretion granted withdrawn MEANS
    `Order under Article 28 as it applies to a charity` WITH
        `the Order categorizes the charity as an organized religious charity` IS categorizes
        `the Order gives the Commissioner discretion to grant or withdraw the status` IS discretion
        `the Commissioner has granted the status` IS granted
        `the Commissioner has withdrawn the status` IS withdrawn

-- A28-04, A28-10: status as an organized religious charity
#ASSERT `Art 28 the entity is an organized religious charity` TRUE (`ind-c Article 28 Order` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 28 the entity is an organized religious charity` TRUE (`ind-c Article 28 Order` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 28 the entity is an organized religious charity` TRUE (`ind-c Article 28 Order` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 28 the entity is an organized religious charity` TRUE (`ind-c Article 28 Order` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `ind-c Articles 29 to 31 -- restricted information`

GIVEN underLaw IS A BOOLEAN
      indirect IS A BOOLEAN
      public IS A BOOLEAN
      summary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Information received and its character`
`ind-c information` underLaw indirect public summary MEANS
    `Information received and its character` WITH
        `relates to the business or other affairs of a person` IS TRUE
        `received under or for the purposes of this Law` IS underLaw
        `received directly or indirectly from a person who so received it` IS indirect
        `already made available to the public from other sources` IS public
        `in the form of a summary or collection that identifies no particular person` IS summary

GIVEN byCommissioner IS A BOOLEAN
      recipient IS A `Recipient of a disclosure of information`
      forCommissioner IS A BOOLEAN
      forRecipient IS A BOOLEAN
      forCharities IS A BOOLEAN
      forOffence IS A BOOLEAN
      forProceedings IS A BOOLEAN
      regulations IS A BOOLEAN
      required IS A BOOLEAN
      subjectConsents IS A BOOLEAN
      sourceConsents IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Disclosure of information`
`ind-c disclosure` byCommissioner recipient forCommissioner forRecipient forCharities forOffence forProceedings regulations required subjectConsents sourceConsents MEANS
    `Disclosure of information` WITH
        `by or on behalf of the Commissioner` IS byCommissioner
        `recipient` IS recipient
        `to enable the Commissioner to discharge a function` IS forCommissioner
        `to enable the recipient to discharge a function` IS forRecipient
        `to enable the recipient to discharge a function in relation to charities` IS forCharities
        `for the investigation or prosecution of an offence` IS forOffence
        `for taking or deciding whether to take proceedings under this Law` IS forProceedings
        `in circumstances prescribed by Regulations` IS regulations
        `required by the recipient for its functions` IS required
        `consent of the person to whom the information relates` IS subjectConsents
        `consent of the person from whom the information was received` IS sourceConsents

`ind-c to a journalist without consent` MEANS `ind-c disclosure` FALSE `a disclosure to any other person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind-c received under the Law` MEANS `ind-c information` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`ind-c received indirectly` MEANS `ind-c information` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN publicPart IS A BOOLEAN
      info IS AN `Information received and its character`
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c offence 29` publicPart info disclosure MEANS
    `Art 29(1) the person commits an offence` `ind-c G8 A` publicPart info disclosure

-- A29-01 (and A29-07, A29-22: the restricted name of a restricted-section charity, to a journalist, no consent)
#ASSERT `ind-c offence 29` FALSE `ind-c received under the Law` `ind-c to a journalist without consent`
